CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract foo --apply-loop-contracts _ --no-standard-checks --unwinding-assertions --unwind 5
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[foo.loop_assigns.\d+\] line 21 Check assigns clause inclusion for loop .*: SUCCESS$
^\[foo.loop_invariant_step.\d+\] line 21 Check invariant after step for loop .*: SUCCESS$
^\[foo.postcondition.\d+\] .* Check ensures clause of contract contract::foo for function foo: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[foo.loop_assigns.\d+\] .*: FAILURE$
^\[foo.assigns.\d+\] .*: FAILURE$
unwinding assertion .*: FAILURE$
--
This test checks that a loop with a contract nested in a loop without a contract
is checked against the write set of the enclosing function, because the outer
loop is not abstracted and has no write set of its own. Furthermore, locals that
the inner loop assigns, whether declared at the top level of the function (`i`)
or inside the outer loop (`x`), must be tracked in the function's write set for
the assigns clause inclusion check of the inner loop to succeed.
